{#- ============================================================================
    v6 "why" — the client's four card designs, placed as images.

    Earlier passes rebuilt these cards in CSS from a Figma export. This one
    stops doing that: the client supplied the cards as rendered images, so the
    section places the images and the browser is no longer asked to
    re-implement a design it kept getting subtly wrong.

    The images are normalised by tools/build_why_cards.py onto a single canvas
    anchored on the card's white body, so all four are the same box with the
    body in the same place (38, 77 at 1x, body 218.96 wide). That is what makes
    them line up: the markup below does not nudge anything per card.

    Sizing: --card-w in 08-v6-why.css is the *body* width, i.e. the size the
    client specified in Figma. The image is wider than the body because the
    tilted plate and the glow lean outside it, so .wfig pulls those overhangs
    back out of the text column with negative margins derived from the same
    canvas geometry. Text and card therefore share one left edge, and changing
    --card-w rescales the whole thing with the aspect ratio locked (the image
    only ever sets a width; height stays auto).

    Accessibility: the figures now live in pixels, so every number is repeated
    in a visually-hidden figcaption, driven off the same content/*.json the CSS
    version used. Screen readers and search engines still get the data, and on
    the English pages that text is English even while the artwork is not.

    Card order is the reference's (chart, silos, lab, route), resolved by
    widget name rather than by reordering capacity.cards, which is also indexed
    positionally by the dispatch radar in tools/build_site.py and by the legacy
    #capacity macro in blocks.html.j2.
    ============================================================================ -#}

{%- macro section() -%}
{%- set card_img = {'chart': 'why-chart', 'bars': 'why-silos', 'lab': 'why-lab', 'orbit': 'why-route'} -%}
{#- The image is laid out at the body's natural width; see .wfig. -#}
{%- set img_sizes = '(max-width: 40rem) 96vw, 301px' -%}
{%- set by_widget = {} -%}
{%- for card in c.capacity.cards %}{% set _ = by_widget.update({card.widget: card}) %}{% endfor -%}
{%- set ordered = [] -%}
{%- for w in ['chart', 'bars', 'lab', 'orbit'] %}{% if w in by_widget %}{% set _ = ordered.append(by_widget[w]) %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- for card in c.capacity.cards %}{% if card not in ordered %}{% set _ = ordered.append(card) %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
<section class="section section--tight why-us" id="why" role="region" aria-labelledby="whyus-t">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="tag tag--lime" data-r>{{ c.capacity.eyebrow }}</span>
      <h2 id="whyus-t" class="h-iconic" data-split>{{ iconic(c.capacity.title_rich) }}</h2>
      <p class="lead" data-r>{{ c.capacity.lead }}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="wcards">
      {%- for card in ordered %}
      {%- set name = card_img[card.widget] %}
      {%- set m = imgs[name] %}
      <article class="wcard" data-card>
        <figure class="wfig">
          <picture>
            <source type="image/avif" srcset="{{ srcset(name, 'avif') }}" sizes="{{ img_sizes }}">
            <img src="{{ p }}assets/img/{{ name }}-{{ m.widths[0] }}.webp"
                 srcset="{{ srcset(name, 'webp') }}" sizes="{{ img_sizes }}"
                 width="{{ m.widths[-1] }}" height="{{ m['h' ~ m.widths[-1]] }}"
                 alt="{{ card.head }} — {{ card.fig }} {{ card.fig_unit }}. {{ card.cap_k }}"
                 loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </picture>
          {#- Every figure the artwork shows, as text. -#}
          <figcaption class="sr">
            {%- if card.widget == 'chart' -%}
            {{ c.a11y.chart_caption }}:
            {%- for s in card.series %} {{ s.year }} — {{ s.v | string | replace('.', decimal) }} {{ card.fig_unit }}
            {%- if s.dry is defined and s.dry %} ({{ card.dry_label }}){% endif %}{{ ';' if not loop.last else '.' }}
            {%- endfor %} {{ card.cap_k }}: {{ card.cap_v }}.
            {%- elif card.widget == 'bars' -%}
            {{ card.cap_k }} — {{ card.cap_v }}.
            {%- for r in card.rows[:2] %} {{ r.name }} — {{ r.val }} ({{ r.pct }}%){{ ';' if not loop.last else '.' }}{% endfor %}
            {%- elif card.widget == 'lab' -%}
            {{ card.cap_k }}, {{ card.fig }} {{ card.fig_unit }}.
            {%- for r in card.rows %} {{ r.name }} — {{ r.val }} {{ r.unit }} ({{ r.trend }}){{ ';' if not loop.last else '.' }}{% endfor %}
            {%- elif card.widget == 'orbit' -%}
            {{ card.cap_k }} — {{ card.cap_v }}.
            {%- for s in card.stops %} {{ s.name }} — {{ s.km }} {{ card.km_unit }}{{ ';' if not loop.last else '.' }}{% endfor %}
            {%- endif -%}
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h3 class="wcard__h3"><span class="wcard__num">{{ '%02d' % loop.index }}</span>{{ card.title }}</h3>
        <p class="wcard__p">{{ card.text }}</p>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endmacro -%}
